{
  "id": "COMPOUND:37553 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Gibberellin A19 may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Gibberellin A19 is directly linked to CD70 antigen, which in turn is targeted by (2S)-1-O-3,6,9,12,15-Octadecapentaenoyl-2-O-6,9,12,15-Octadecatetraenoyl-3-O-Beta-D-Galactopyranosylsn-Glycerol, a compound that ultimately targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, Gibberellin A19 is also associated with CD70 antigen, which is targeted by lidocaine, another compound that directly interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings collectively suggest that Gibberellin A19 may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its interaction with CD70 antigen, which serves as a bridge to the target complex. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Gibberellin A19 modulates the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex via CD70 antigen, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
